  "changes": [
    "Current batch 32 now uses a source-locked JSON refinement through the same template-pinning, compiler and runtime fixtures as the other heroes. The legacy Azazel function and tests remain explicitly frozen old-version compatibility evidence; they are not counted as current-batch semantic proof.",
    "PASSIVE earns at most one negative-energy mark per real paid cast that damages enemy HP, across targets and waves. It caps at three and resets by round. Self-damage, zero/immune/fully shielded contacts, raw packets lacking a cast identity and hook reflections cannot create a cast credit.",
    "Q has a two-unit range, a 0.2-second interruptible windup, one physical punch and 0.4 units of knockback. W re-resolves a fixed 2.75-unit landing area for three waves 0.45 seconds apart, one hit per target per wave and one energy credit total. Death or settled combat cancels pending rain.",
    "E grants a 0.5-second, caster-owned counter window. Its mutually exclusive basic/ability hooks require positive HP or shield loss from an enemy within 2.5 units, then deliver one normal physical shadow punch and remove the window. Incoming damage is not negated; there is no undocumented front-only condition. Zero/immune, distant, friendly, cross-duel, hook and expired contacts do not consume it. Counter packets use normal damage multipliers and cannot consume another counter window or earn energy.",
    "R keeps its 0.8-second charge, successful-launch 3% maximum-life cost with a one-HP floor, and actual projectile hit. Its four-second curse now changes outputDamagePct by -0.15 using a flat modifier rather than AD/AP; fixed damage is truly reduced. Healing and shield output axes are unchanged.",
    "EX atomically pays three marks. An own-source R curse is removed and replaced by a two-second +0.10 damage-output boon without ordinary EX damage. Missing, cleansed or expired own curse instead gives normal EX damage and a two-second -0.20 output curse. Another caster's R remains independent. THE END OF SON R→EX reversal is preserved and proven with genuinely earned resources.",
    "A generic distance condition now rejects entities in different duel zones for every comparison operator, consistent with the existing facing condition. It no longer lets a close-hit counter act across duels.",
    "The trusted importer runs the current authored whole kit, earning its EX marks without seeding. Editor prior-R preview establishes the actual curse; ready-resource setup remains explicitly labelled and empty-resource preview still refuses with only one earned mark. Template and project clones stay isolated.",
    "The existing Azazel-specific handoff command now reads the same versioned refinement JSON as the bulk command. Both independently rebuilt all 37 projects with byte-identical results; old originals, models and rollback versions remain available."
  ],
